---
// About: site.md §4, copy verbatim. The /review style (Site.astro), one column of short paragraphs down the right.
// Photo: one shot, an asymmetric crop, mid-size (design notes §4), in the left column beside the text and held there
// while the text scrolls. It shows once a file is in src/assets/about/; until then the column stays empty.
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import Site from "../layouts/Site.astro";

const photos = import.meta.glob<{ default: ImageMetadata }>("../assets/about/*.{jpg,jpeg,png,webp}", { eager: true });
const photo = Object.values(photos)[0]?.default;
---

<Site title="About" description="I design products. I've been doing it for five years." image="/review-og.png">
  <main class="page about">
    <section class="row intro">
      <h1 class="label caps">ABOUT</h1>
      <p class="title">I'm Nikita.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="row">
      {
        photo ? (
          <figure class="photo">
            <Image src={photo} alt="Nikita Filippov" widths={[400, 800]} sizes="(min-width: 900px) 330px, 70vw" />
          </figure>
        ) : (
          <span class="label" aria-hidden="true" />
        )
      }
      <div class="text">
        <p class="lead"><span>I design products.</span> <span>I've been doing it for five&nbsp;years.</span></p>
        <p>I studied business, not design. I started designing because of a project of my own: I felt nobody else would get how I wanted it to look. Then came work for friends, then a website for a local repair and tailoring shop. It's still&nbsp;live.</p>
        <p>Then Medal, a desktop app for gamers. I worked on avatars and rewards, then on how you record the thing that just happened. Then crypto: a wallet, an explorer, a set of tools. The wallet launched at ETHDenver 2023. The explorer never shipped. None of it runs now, for reasons that had nothing to do with&nbsp;design.</p>
        <p>I've worked in teams and in a studio. Now I design on my own. The work I'm proudest of came when the decisions were mine to&nbsp;make.</p>

        <hr class="rule" />

        <p>I like to travel, change my surroundings and get deep into a culture I don't know&nbsp;yet.</p>
        <p>I reply to designers on X more than I post. I build my own tools with Claude&nbsp;Code. I'm trying to make design experiments a habit, and to post each&nbsp;one.</p>

        <hr class="rule" />

        <div class="closing">
          <p>That's about it.<br />If you want to work together —</p>
          <a class="btn" href="/review/" data-gem>Send a link, get a video review <span class="arw">→</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Site>

<style>
  .intro {
    padding-top: 40px;
    align-items: baseline;
  }
  .title {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(40px, 5.6vw, 80px);
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 0.98;
    letter-spacing: -0.058em;
  }

  /* The photo holds its place in the left column while the text scrolls past it. */
  .photo {
    position: sticky;
    top: 24px;
    width: min(330px, 100%);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .photo :global(img) {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 28px;
    box-shadow: var(--float);
  }

  .text {
    display: grid;
    gap: 22px;
    max-width: 31em;
  }
  .text p {
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.5;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  .text .lead {
    font-size: var(--text-lead);
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.05em;
  }
  /* Each sentence starts its own line. */
  .text .lead span {
    display: block;
  }
  .rule {
    margin: 40px 0;
  }
  .closing {
    margin-top: 8px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .photo {
      position: static;
      width: min(300px, 78%);
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .intro {
      padding-top: 16px;
    }
    .title {
      font-size: 36px;
    }
    .text .lead {
      font-size: 24px;
    }
    .rule {
      margin: 24px 0;
    }
  }
</style>
